    "problem_statement": "Or() validation broken after initialization changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `Or` class is not working correctly after recent changes to its initialization. When trying to validate data with `Or()`, it fails to match any values even when they should be valid.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom schema import Schema, Or\n\n# Simple Or validation fails\nschema = Schema(Or(1, 2, 3))\nresult = schema.validate(2)  # Should pass but raises SchemaError\n\n# Or with types also fails\nschema = Schema(Or(str, int))\nresult = schema.validate(\"hello\")  # Should pass but raises SchemaError\n\n# List validation with Or fails\nschema = Schema([Or(str, int)])\nresult = schema.validate([\"hello\", 42])  # Should pass but raises SchemaError\n```\n\nThe validation fails with errors like:\n```\nschema.SchemaError: Or() did not validate 2\nschema.SchemaError: Or('error', 'error') did not validate ['hello', 42]\n```\n\nThis affects basic `Or` functionality across the library, including dictionary key validation and nested schema validation."
  }
